1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting
sun over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoes flew off too,

3
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
and everyone laughed that
I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase after some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
sighs and yawns, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat's water fountain,

9
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:07,460
the sun sinks into the vast sky.

10
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow will end just like this too,
won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,720
Katsushika, Shibamata, happy again,

12
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:24,500
because I'm a fool who only
realized after the fact.

13
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,660
Wani-ko, tears of a comedian's spirit.

14
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,800
Only 3 yen until payday.

15
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:44,000
I can't even afford a lottery ticket at the candy store,
let alone anything else.

16
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:46,580
Look at this.

17
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:48,980
Just a single one-yen coin.

18
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,060
Even if it becomes 4 yen,
it's still not enough.

19
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:54,440
I'm holding...

20
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:54,740
Mm.

21
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:06,360
Today's machine has continuous spinning with no stopping point.
Everyone can enjoy it to their heart's content

22
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:09,880
That's perfect. This is the result
of that genre hitting its limit.

23
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,020
Thank you for coming in, as always.

24
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:13,080
Mm.

25
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:19,600
Wh-what, seriously!?

26
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:26,060
Alright, busy, busy!
We're closing up today, closing up!

27
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:28,020
Why are you closing in
the middle of the day?

28
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:32,360
A typhoon is coming,
so we're closing up for today.

29
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,840
Too bad, sir.

30
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,320
As if a typhoon is going to come!

31
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:42,220
These two are former aces of
the soccer and basketball clubs.

32
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,340
They're defense professionals.

33
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:57,420
Come on, manager,
you can sell me a million, can't you?

34
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:00,080
That's offside, manager.

35
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:04,000
Give me one ball.

36
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,480
We don't sell the balls
individually, though.

37
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:10,280
These are all the seeds there are.
Just sell me some somehow.

38
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:13,860
Well, please don't make
unreasonable demands.

39
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,140
You can buy eggs one at a time, can't you!

40
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:20,720
Even milk comes in 1-liter,
500ml, or 250ml sizes these days!

41
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,340
Pachinko parlors have to
meet consumer needs too!

42
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:24,920
N-no way...

43
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,940
Even a master couldn't do it in one shot.

44
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,120
Alright then.

45
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:32,700
Understood.

46
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:35,800
If it's over in one shot,
you'll leave right away, won't you?

47
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,720
Of course.

48
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,180
And no picking up fallen
balls to shoot them, either.

49
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,120
F-fine.

50
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:42,620
You promise, right?

51
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:49,720
If you fail, you absolutely must go home.
Now, hurry up and get this gentleman set up.

52
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:54,520
Shoot one for him. Here you go.
It's a one-shot showdown with the genius.

53
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:03,060
Now, which machine should I pick?

54
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,740
First, that one's an open machine.

55
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:18,140
Phew, I walked right past the open machine.

56
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:26,460
Maybe I'll go with this one after all.

57
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:30,680
Seriously, my face is being read. Stay calm.

58
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:38,040
No, wait, that machine over there
looks like it's about to pay out.

59
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:39,840
Right.

60
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:40,080
Hah.

61
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:44,440
I just can't stop thinking
about that machine.

62
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,680
1, 2, 3, 4

63
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:49,100
1, 2, 3, 4

64
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:49,920
This one?

65
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:51,040
That one?

66
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:52,460
This one?

67
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,200
Maybe that one after all.

68
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,240
But this one, then.

69
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:58,840
No, I can't do this, stop!

70
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:04,260
A manager should at least
practice keeping a poker face.

71
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:08,520
Go!

72
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:16,240
Alright!

73
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:25,860
Yes!

74
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:31,020
Hide the valuable prizes, quick!

75
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:34,300
They'll take everything! Hide them, hurry!

76
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:40,080
There are 527,235 of them.

77
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:43,940
For starters, five cases of
juice and ten boxes of biscuits.

78
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:48,160
Then, twenty cases each of yakiniku canned meat,
crab cans, and corned beef.

79
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:51,338
A year's supply of toilet
paper and 100 pairs of underwear,

80
00:05:51,388 --> 00:05:54,380
one sack of rice, and one top-grade each of miso,
soy sauce, and sake.

81
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:57,320
And for the consolation prizes,
I'll take about thirty wristwatches too.

82
00:05:57,340 --> 00:06:00,020
If I take them to the pawnshop,
they'll help cover living expenses.

83
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:03,340
Have everything delivered to me later,
would you?

84
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,000
How many are left?

85
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:08,100
About 300,000 still.

86
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,580
Please, have mercy!
If the prizes run out, our business...

87
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:16,940
Don't you have anything else?

88
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:19,920
What about that?

89
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:23,740
Yes, I run a pet shop on the side. Yes.

90
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:30,080
If you'd like, I can offer you a pet of
your choice with the remaining 300,000.

91
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:32,660
A pet

92
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:40,900
Ryotsu's late again

93
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:45,220
Can't he even show up properly the day after payday?
Honestly.

94
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,940
Looks like he's here.

95
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,720
Hey, Ryotsu! What time do you think it is?

96
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,500
Good morning.

97
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:59,300
Ryotsu, what's that?

98
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:02,480
Does this look like a
surfboard to you, Chief?

99
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:04,060
It's a crocodile, a crocodile!

100
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:05,540
Isn't he cute?

101
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:07,880
What a docile crocodile.

102
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:09,880
You're not even surprised?

103
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:13,160
Geez, don't scare me like that, senpai.

104
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:15,880
It's a really well-made fake, isn't it?

105
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:17,340
Go on, poke it, I'm telling you.

106
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:19,340
It's the real thing!

107
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:24,240
I haven't fed him yet this morning,
so getting close is dangerous.

108
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:27,040
W-you should have told me that first!

109
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,020
It's delicious peach meat, you know.

110
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:34,700
Chew it up really well, okay?

111
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:41,300
Keep him by your side and feed him,
and he's a well-behaved little guy.

112
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:44,160
He won't cause any more trouble than the edge of a...
well, anyone else.

113
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,120
Good boy, good boy.

114
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:49,940
He was nuzzling and rubbing up against me.

115
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:55,300
Ryotsu, you're not seriously planning
to keep that crocodile, are you?

116
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:59,060
Of course I am, Chief Ohara!

117
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:04,500
Because keeping a crocodile has
been my dream since I was a child!

118
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:06,760
I've never heard you say that before.

119
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:09,480
Why a crocodile instead of a dog or a cat?

120
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:12,960
This guy's character,
which people easily misunderstand,

121
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:15,360
I really can't think of him as a stranger.

122
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,916
Please, take a look,

123
00:08:16,966 --> 00:08:20,660
at the round eyes of this
fierce-looking crocodile.

124
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:22,580
You don't have to do that.

125
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:23,440
Well.

126
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,560
Stop, Ryo-chan! It'll bite you!

127
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:28,940
Ryo-chan!

128
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:30,987
Those sharp fangs are used

129
00:08:31,037 --> 00:08:34,200
to protect itself from
enemies and to catch prey.

130
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,820
It would never attack
a person in the dark...

131
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:38,800
S-Senpai!

132
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,160
He's just playing around, that's all.

133
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:52,160
What a cute little crocodile.

134
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,540
There you go.

135
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:56,800
Chu-chu-chu!

136
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:58,260
Hey, stop struggling, hey!

137
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:01,820
Scrub, scrub, scrub.

138
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:05,240
Come on, little croc,
let's get you nice and clean.

139
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:08,260
So your back gets a nice shine.

140
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:13,160
Don't put him down, you know.

141
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:16,540
Come on, let's get under his arms clean too.

142
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:23,300
Maybe Ryo-chan is surprisingly
good at taking care of animals.

143
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:30,420
Post-bath wax,
and it's two rounds of sleeping in today.

144
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,700
What, are you hungry already?

145
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:40,260
Right, right,
growing kids get hungry, don't they?

146
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,320
There, there,
eat lots and grow up fast, okay?

147
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:47,880
Little Croc-chan, you're all shiny now!

148
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:52,860
If you spoil him like a cat that much, he
won't grow into a decent crocodile, Ryotsu.

149
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:58,020
It's fine. From today on, I'm devoting myself
to the crocodile with an animal-welfare spirit.

150
00:09:58,020 --> 00:10:02,320
I'll fight abnormal weather and shady business
practices and aim for administrative reform.

151
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,860
Administrative reform?

152
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:06,900
Sounds like there's something behind that.

153
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:07,840
Yeah.

154
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:12,960
Eat plenty and grow up fast, okay?

155
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,160
Six of them

156
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:24,920
Good, good.

157
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:25,900
Fifty percent off.

158
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:27,860
You certainly have a good eye.

159
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,320
A crocodile handbag.

160
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:33,240
This one alone costs over 500,000 yen.

161
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,860
Is it expensive because it's crocodile?

162
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:36,920
Yes.

163
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:40,620
Of course.

164
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:46,660
If you raise this crocodile for five years,
it grows to about five meters and sells for around four million yen.

165
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:49,400
You're guaranteed to make a profit.

166
00:10:55,900 --> 00:11:02,980
Four million, four million, that's just how it is.
What, what, what's with all of you?

167
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:11,420
What do you mean
"that's how it is," Nakagawa? You're raising crocodiles just for their hide and planning to sell them for 4 million, aren't you?

168
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,440
Ugh.

169
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:23,280
So I knew it. The manager's only after the money,
isn't he?

170
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:28,180
I was a fool to think you'd
woken up to animal welfare.

171
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:32,100
Are you saying people keep chickens, cows, and pigs as pets?
How heartless!

172
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:35,760
They all raise them to sell,
to make a living, right?

173
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:36,560
Well, that's...

174
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:39,900
What's wrong with raising
crocodiles to make a living?

175
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:43,100
I'm keeping this one as a moving piggy bank.

176
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,340
The crocodile's gone!

177
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:46,220
The crocodile went toward the kitchen!

178
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:47,780
What's wrong?

179
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:49,460
Look at that!

180
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,080
That crocodile is standing on two legs!

181
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:57,040
Hey, wait a second -

182
00:11:57,040 --> 00:12:00,400
that's everyone's meat we
bought for our late-night snack!

183
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,240
It wouldn't eat it, would it?

184
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,880
Stop it, Reiko.

185
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:07,260
But the crocodile ate everyone's meat -

186
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,940
I'll pay you back for the meat.

187
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:13,160
But in return, don't mistreat my
precious crocodile from now on.

188
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:14,000
Got it?

189
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:17,640
That crocodile is laughing at us!

190
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,620
Don't make fun of us!

191
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:25,820
Another walk

192
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:28,400
Honestly, it's so carefree.

193
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:30,380
Where do you think you're going?

194
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:32,340
Hey, hey.

195
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,060
Welcome!

196
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:38,900
This is the famous, expensive butcher shop.

197
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,360
What can I get for you?

198
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,640
No, I'm fine today.

199
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:45,480
Gah!

200
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:49,280
Gah, 4,000 yen per kilo!

201
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:51,140
Don't say it!

202
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:54,160
The cheap ones here,
three slices with plenty of meat.

203
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:59,600
Sooner or later,
it'll all become blood and flesh.

204
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,320
A handbag for 4 million!

205
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:03,800
Should I just overlook a little luxury?

206
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,600
This fillet here.

207
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:08,360
100 grams.

208
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:13,620
One kilo, please.

209
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:28,400
Four thousand yen for fillet

210
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:35,040
To me, he's my pet,
so a little selfishness can't be helped.

211
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:39,480
They said he'd be worth a
million yen in five years, right?

212
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:44,180
So how much was all the meat
you fed the crocodile today?

213
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:52,120
If I recall, the thigh meat was 3 kilos for 2,940 yen,
so together that's 7,000 yen

214
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:54,520
And what about what Reiko-san ate?

215
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:57,540
Loin is 200 yen per 100 grams,
so that's 1,000 yen's worth.

216
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:03,020
Even a rough calculation,
the feed costs come to 240,000 yen a month!

217
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:05,940
Then we'd be losing money, wouldn't we?

218
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:08,500
What did you just say?

219
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,740
The crocodile sells for 4 million?

220
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:17,518
Forget the tenderloin,

221
00:14:17,568 --> 00:14:20,860
keep the feed costs low, at 100,000 a month,

222
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:25,413
that's 1.2 million in a year,
6 million in five years,

223
00:14:25,463 --> 00:14:28,180
so after subtracting costs,
it's minus 2 million!

224
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:29,940
Senpai...

225
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:31,740
Instead of savings, we'd be in debt!

226
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:34,600
Time to say goodbye!

227
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:42,540
Shut up!

228
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:45,860
That pachinko parlor tricked us!

229
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:56,900
Ew, it stinks!

230
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:01,741
The more we buy,
the deeper we go into the red.

231
00:15:01,791 --> 00:15:03,100
This is outrageous!

232
00:15:05,220 --> 00:15:07,480
I don't need your sympathy!

233
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:13,680
Now that we know it's a loss,
we have no reason or money to buy you!

234
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:18,940
Get out of my sight right now!
Become a stray crocodile for all of you!

235
00:15:27,700 --> 00:15:30,580
If the crocodile causes trouble,
you'll be fired too, senpai.

236
00:15:30,580 --> 00:15:31,880
Why would I get fired?

237
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:34,080
The one to blame is this idiot, right?

238
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:38,980
Once you've decided to keep a pet,
the owner has a duty to take care of it.

239
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:39,820
Ryo-chan.

240
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,980
You good-for-nothing who only
knows how to eat and sleep!

241
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:44,800
This ugly thing doesn't deserve to be a pet!

242
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,120
You parasite!

243
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:51,860
This crocodile is awfully flexible,
isn't it?

244
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:55,460
Even if the crocodile does a bridge,
it won't earn us a single yen.

245
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:59,780
But I've never seen a crocodile like this.
It's really cute, isn't it?

246
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:01,260
What?

247
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,560
Can it do anything else?

248
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:17,700
Hey, this might just work.

249
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:18,920
Hey,

250
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:20,680
Hey, look.

251
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,360
Don't kid yourself.

252
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:26,580
Until it makes money,
it gets nothing but bird feed.

253
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:34,400
And this week's top prize goes to...

254
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:37,380
Genius Croc-kun!

255
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:39,220
We're presenting the
grand prize of 100,000 yen!

256
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:40,020
We did it, Wani-ko!

257
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:42,400
It's 100,000 yen in prize money!

258
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,240
Okay, okay, I get it.

259
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:54,300
This could be a moneymaker.

260
00:16:57,420 --> 00:17:00,420
That crocodile who showed off
riding a bike in the triangle style,

261
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:02,460
the first prize is 100,000 yen.

262
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:07,480
Mr. Croc.

263
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:10,900
Today I'll let you eat real meat for once.

264
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:14,460
But it's the cheapest pork scraps.

265
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:18,860
If you want fancier meat,
go earn more prize money.

266
00:17:18,860 --> 00:17:21,280
You have to earn your own living expenses.

267
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,260
Got it?

268
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:23,880
Mm.

269
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:30,240
Well th-this...

270
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:32,744
Good, loin,

271
00:17:32,794 --> 00:17:36,200
extra bone-in short ribs, ten servings each!

272
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:38,562
once again, the winner is Wani-kun,

273
00:17:38,612 --> 00:17:40,680
amazingly, four weeks in a row!

274
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:44,836
Old man, give me all the
plastic models on this plate,

275
00:17:44,886 --> 00:17:46,600
Heh, I've got the money.

276
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:55,860
The bicycle gag is
probably getting old by now.

277
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:01,500
Find some other gag or something.

278
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:05,880
No matter how you look at it, it's amazing.

279
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:09,400
Master craftsmanship never gets old,
does it?

280
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:14,560
Yes, I'm riding along. Everyone,
please give a big round of applause!

281
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,280
Eeeeeh!

282
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:20,560
Eeeeeh!

283
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:30,760
Eeeeeeh?

284
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,100
Eeeeeeh?

285
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:32,080
Eeeeeeh?

286
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:32,540
Eeeeeeh?

287
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:32,620
Eeeeeeh?

288
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:39,780
Hey, Reiko.

289
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:42,640
Did you get any calls from
TV stations or anything?

290
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,000
No, nothing.

291
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:44,940
Why not?

292
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:47,840
After what they put me through
on that amateur video show.

293
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:51,740
It's about time I got a call from show business,
don't you think?

294
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,320
Will it really go that smoothly?

295
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,520
There they are, over here!

296
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,240
That's the big brother?

297
00:18:57,820 --> 00:18:58,720
What do you lot want?

298
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:00,740
Excuse me.

299
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:06,940
We'd actually like to ask
Wani-kun to appear on our show.

300
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:10,740
Of course,
we plan to provide plenty of meat as well.

301
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,620
I see.

302
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,340
If that's the case,

303
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:20,600
I, Manager Bin-Wan, will hear you out.

304
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,900
Especially the appearance fee, of course.

305
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:26,220
What the hell do you think you're doing?

306
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:31,540
You're the worst.

307
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:38,260
You're fired? Why?

308
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:42,000
If they take ninety percent in kickbacks,
even a crocodile would be angry, Ryo-san.

309
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,720
Damn, getting so full of yourself.

310
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:50,240
But that guy is our precious golden crane.

311
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:52,460
We can't let him go now.

312
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:58,060
Please, Mr. Crocodile,

313
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:00,020
don't get us fired, please.

314
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:07,180
This week's number one is
the wildly popular Mr. Croc!

315
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:14,020
Little Croc, you're wonderful!

316
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:17,480
It's been a while since
we've met face to face.

317
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:22,940
I've missed you.
You've become so impressive.

318
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:27,020
You lying bastard of a manager!

319
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:59,600
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

320
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:02,020
Hey, you lot, don't peek!

321
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:03,860
The teacher is exhausted, you know.

322
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:06,300
Here you go, coffee.

323
00:21:06,660 --> 00:21:09,000
Honestly,
these high school girls these days.

324
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:15,920
Sorry.

325
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:18,260
We only had inserts, so...

326
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:19,680
We'll reinsert it right away.

327
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:25,300
I remember, Wanico.

328
00:21:29,980 --> 00:21:32,200
Senpai, you're really holding back,
aren't you?

329
00:21:32,660 --> 00:21:36,460
Ryo-san is greedy too,
so they're evenly matched.

330
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:40,360
Wow, it's a Wanipin!

331
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:43,660
Wani-chan's been on TV a lot lately,
hasn't she?

332
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:48,740
But if she's on constantly like this, people
will get tired of her quickly, won't they?

333
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:53,420
For the new show,
we'd really love to have our crocodile.

334
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:57,080
We've already settled on other cast members.

335
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,680
No, please, somehow... ah...

336
00:21:59,940 --> 00:22:00,780
It's finished.

337
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:03,520
Damn, this one's no good either.

338
00:22:04,500 --> 00:22:04,860
Yes.

339
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:07,720
Yes, that's right.

340
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:09,460
The crocodile's been cancelled?

341
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:10,580
Are you already tired of it?

342
00:22:11,220 --> 00:22:13,240
Don't say that, please, I'm begging you.

343
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:16,140
Look, the schedule's completely blank.

344
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:19,320
There's zero work coming up.

345
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:21,980
I've got no use for someone
who doesn't make money.

346
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:26,520
I'm quitting as your manager,
effective today.

347
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:27,520
Well then, goodbye.

348
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,060
Your act has been tossed
aside by the public.

349
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:39,960
Figure out what to do with Asou yourself.

350
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:41,760
I want nothing more to do with you.

351
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:54,900
Sorry I'm late, Chief.

352
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,140
Aren't you thoughtful.

353
00:23:00,340 --> 00:23:01,540
What do you think you're doing?

354
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:03,500
Thanks, Wani-chan.

355
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:05,580
Chief, why is this guy here?

356
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:07,320
Late again?

357
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:09,180
Ryotsu, you're living the high life,
aren't you.

358
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:12,600
Getting Wani-chan to help you with all
sorts of things since this morning...

359
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:14,280
I was really saved.

360
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:17,200
They do say a temple boy learns
sutras without being taught.

361
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:21,440
Apparently he picked up
police box duties in no time.

362
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:23,800
He's far more capable than Ryotsu.

363
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:27,480
Damn it.

364
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,740
Right, Chief.
Shall I massage your shoulders?

365
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:34,320
Wani-kun already massaged
my shoulders earlier.

366
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:37,820
Your transparent little act
is painful to watch, Ryotsu.

367
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:41,360
Excuse me, which way is Kameari Station?

368
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:51,440
With Wani-kun here,
you're not needed, Ryotsu.

369
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:56,040
Please do something about it.

370
00:23:57,480 --> 00:23:58,700
Well, I can't tell you that!

371
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:09,540
The loan collectors, good for nothing else,
are going to face off in a baseball match for the honor of the shopping district.

372
00:24:09,540 --> 00:24:14,880
But since I'm their ringer now, I'll
win no matter what dirty tricks it takes!

373
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:17,940
And you lot, don't forget that promise!

374
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:21,580
Next time, the storm-summoning baseball tournament.
Look forward to it!

375
00:24:30,580 --> 00:24:37,240
Though people gossip that I'm
a woman who can't fall in love,

376
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:42,420
I have a mountain of things I want to do.

377
00:24:42,420 --> 00:24:52,040
I want to ride my motorbike
across the vast desert.

378
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:59,180
I want to be freer than the birds.

379
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,140
A lady's dreams that change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

380
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:07,700
Me

381
00:25:07,700 --> 00:25:09,860
Me

382
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:11,680
Me

383
00:25:13,140 --> 00:25:14,060
Me

384
00:25:19,900 --> 00:25:21,300
Me

385
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:25,000
Me

386
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:25,900
Me

387
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:28,340
Me

388
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:29,440
Me

389
00:25:35,060 --> 00:25:36,460
Me

390
00:25:38,140 --> 00:25:41,060
Thank you for watching.

